  "notes": "Modified cash basis village. Governmental lines from the governmental funds statement, 2023 Total Governmental Funds column (pp4-5); it rolls fund balances 655,044 -> 571,553 (fund balance fields). Ending cash 562,576 is the governmental funds Cash line (p3); beginning cash left null (only a 2022 comparative column showing 1,100,166 with large interfund balances). 'Grant revenue' row is a dash in 2023 (not recorded). Business-type (Water, Sewer) lines from the modified cash proprietary statement (p7), which ties to the Statement of Activities (p2): operating revenues 246,293, expenses 254,968 + interest 3,202 = 258,170 (p2 total business-type expenses), capital grants 10,000 as business_type.other_financing; net position 1,183,559 -> 1,181,682 (p2). Sewer 'Other operating revenues' 1,144 is counted in charges for services on p2. Proprietary cash flow statement (p8) not recorded (GAAP-only field). Balance sheet: governmental lines from the governmental funds statement (p3, totals equal the government-wide governmental column 571,553), business-type lines from the Statement of Net Position business-type column (p1); total_* from the 2023 Total column (p1). Detail: budgetary comparison schedules for all funds (pp9-16). Funds with a single expenditure line or no 'Total revenues' line (Park, Keno, Police revenues, Debt Service expenditure, Water revenue) have no printed per-section total except as noted; 'Total available resources' lines include the beginning balance and are not recorded. Zero-actual lines with budgets (Street 'Bond warrants', Police personal services/repairs/transfers, Debt Service miscellaneous, Water bond and loan proceeds) recorded with amount 0. Read pages 1-16 of 16"
